**Abstract:**

As data sharing becomes increasingly prevalent across various domains, ensuring secure and private data exchange is crucial. Our proposed research aims to develop an innovative access control framework that leverages the concept of data cubes to protect sensitive information shared among multiple agents. By integrating our expertise in data mining and attack graphs with the principles of multi-agent systems, we aim to create a robust and adaptive access control mechanism that balances security and privacy.

